# Win98SE / MS-DOS 7.1 boot-image download source (TEMPLATE).
#
# Copy this file to "w98se.url" in this same folder and put your download URL
# on a line below. When tools\w98se.img is missing, the QEMU harnesses
# (xhciqual\test\run-qemu-matrix.ps1 and run-win98-batch.ps1) fetch the image
# from that URL. This repo hardcodes NO source - the image is proprietary and
# you choose where to get it from.
#
# Equivalent alternatives to this file:
#   - pass -BootImageUrl <url> to a harness, or
#   - set $env:XHCIQUAL_WIN98_URL
# Optional integrity check: set $env:XHCIQUAL_WIN98_SHA256 to the expected hash.
#
# The URL must point to an AUTOMATION-READY image: a bare Win98SE / MS-DOS 7.1
# boot floppy that boots straight to a DOS prompt (no boot menu, no DATE/TIME
# prompt). See xhciqual\README.md ("The Win98 boot image") for how to build one
# from a stock Win98 boot floppy with mtools.
#
# The first non-comment, non-blank line is used as the URL. Uncomment and edit:
# https://example.com/path/to/your/w98se.img
